From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 52/55] scp: report a skipped unwritable destination as a
 failure with -Z

When the destination file could not be written, the "scp -Z" sink printed
"Permission denied", answered with a skip, and went on, so scp exited 0 and the
caller was told the copy had worked although the file was not updated. Count it
as an error so the exit status is not 0. The protocol is unchanged.
---
 scp.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scp.c b/scp.c
index c1f4a60d9..fff4a4484 100644
--- a/scp.c
+++ b/scp.c
@@ -2371,6 +2371,8 @@ sink(int argc, char **argv, const char *src)
 				 * because using a define isn't working */
 				if (access (np, W_OK) != 0) {
 					fprintf(stderr, "scp: %s: Permission denied on %s\n", np, hostname);
+					/* the file was not updated: the exit status says so */
+					++errs;
 					snprintf(outbuf, BUF_AND_HASH, "S%-*s", BUF_AND_HASH-2, " ");
 					(void)atomicio(vwrite, remout, outbuf, strlen(outbuf));
 					(void)atomicio(vwrite, remout, "", 1);
